    "title": "Caught-on-camera: Man seen abandoning cats in STL alley - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Max Diekneite ,\n55 minutes ago ST. LOUIS – FOX 2 is hearing from a resident who said his cameras captured a man dumping cats in the alley of a south St. Louis neighborhood.\nTower Grove East neighbor Rob Day said he couldn’t believe what he’d just witnessed. Day said it happened around 2 p.m. Sunday in the alley behind his home on Pennsylvania Avenue.\nHe said he was taking out his trash as he noticed four cats running through the alley after a red sedan drove off. Three of them appeared to be fully declawed.\nDay shared footage of the incident with FOX 2. It revealed that the driver of the red Hyundai sedan with missing plates backed-into the alley, pulled the four cats out of a cage in the car and drove off.\nClose Thanks for signing up!\nWatch for us in your inbox.\nSubscribe Now\nDaily News Day said he and his partner were able to grab two of the cats. They’re still working to find the other two.\nThe two cats they did recover – a tiger-striped tabby and a younger, black-and-white cat they’ve named “Oreo,” are on the mend. The couple has also set up a GoFundMe to raise money for vet visits and other essentials for the cats.\nDay said they’ve been in contact with police and are hoping someone will be able to identify the driver of the red car.\nKnowingly abandoning animals in Missouri is classified as Animal Neglect , a Class C misdemeanor which could carry fines and penalties.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to FOX 2.",
